  <h1>About Daily Insight Desk</h1>
  <p class="dek">A small home-and-garden desk for readers in the United States. The promise is a clear answer to a real chore, not a pile of products.</p>
  <p>Daily Insight Desk is operated by Etern Digital. The site used to be a short list of product picks. It is now a guide to <a href="/cleaning/">cleaning</a>, the <a href="/kitchen/">kitchen</a>, the <a href="/outdoor/">yard</a>, and the <a href="/tools/">tools</a> those jobs share. The audience is American households, and the writing is in American English.</p>
  <h2>How a guide gets written</h2>
  <p>We start with the task. Published examples are <a href="/cleaning/garden-hose-pressure-nozzle/">what a garden-hose nozzle can rinse</a>, <a href="/cleaning/garment-steamer-vs-iron/">when a steamer is enough</a>, <a href="/kitchen/do-titanium-cutting-boards-dull-knives/">whether a titanium board dulls a knife</a>, and <a href="/kitchen/are-rolling-knife-sharpeners-good/">whether a rolling sharpener is worth owning</a>. We say what the job needs, what it does not need, and where a product is only one option. If a claim comes from a manufacturer, we call it a seller’s claim. If it comes from another publication, we name the publication, the author, and the date. We link out only to non-commercial sources, such as a government or university page or a maker’s own care instructions. A magazine product review that sends readers to a store is cited in plain text. We do not invent tests, statistics, or testimonials.</p>
  <p>We do not publish invented statistics, fabricated testimonials, or medical claims. A cutting board guide can talk about washing a board. It cannot tell you a surface will keep you healthy.</p>
  <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
  <p>Some links are affiliate links. If you buy through one, we may earn a commission, and the price you pay is the seller’s price. Those links use <code>rel="sponsored"</code>. A short note sits just before the first offer link in a guide, and the footer also carries the disclosure. Editorial choices are not a receipt for the commission. A product can be mentioned with a clear limitation, including “this is the wrong tool for the job you think you are buying it for.”</p>
  <p>The full terms are on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>. Questions about an order, a refund, or a shipment belong to the store that took the payment. We do not have those records.</p>
  <h2>What is not here yet</h2>
  <p>Most of the guide list is still ahead. Shelf pages name those upcoming pieces and do not link them, so you are never sent to a missing page. A newsletter is planned and is not open. We are not collecting email addresses until there is a letter to send.</p>
  <h2>Write to us</h2>
  <p>Corrections are welcome. If a sentence is wrong, say so. Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>, or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
